### 8. Responsive Design

The desktop screenshot is the starting point, not the only supported layout.

Build and validate:
- Desktop.
- Tablet.
- Mobile.

On smaller screens:
- Reflow multi-column sections into an appropriate single-column or compact layout.
- Keep text readable without horizontal scrolling.
- Resize decorative section numbers so they do not overwhelm the content.
- Rework overlapping panels instead of simply shrinking the desktop composition.
- Ensure project images retain appropriate aspect ratios and focal points.
- Make buttons, links, and navigation easy to use with touch.
- Keep the hero headline, selected projects, and contact CTA prominent.
- Prevent clipped text, overlapping content, and accidental overflow.
- Make the beige contact section feel consistent with the rest of the page.

Do not treat mobile responsiveness as an afterthought or create a separate visual identity for mobile.

