### 9. Accessibility and Usability

Implement the website with accessibility in mind.

Requirements:
- Semantic HTML and appropriate heading hierarchy.
- Accessible navigation and interactive controls.
- Descriptive link labels.
- Meaningful alternative text for informative images.
- Empty alternative text for purely decorative images where appropriate.
- Sufficient color contrast.
- Visible keyboard-focus states.
- Keyboard-accessible navigation and project links.
- Appropriate form labels and error feedback if a contact form is implemented.
- Reduced-motion support.
- No essential information communicated only through color or hover.
- No tiny text that becomes unreadable on mobile.

Prefer a simple, understandable user experience over unnecessary technical complexity.

